Capybara ETL pipeline to join products with inventory, calculate days_of_stock, filter urgent items, and sort by urgency.

### Changes
- Created a Capybara graph-form pipeline using SOURCE/STEP/SINK/FLOW
- Joined products and inventory on product_id (INNER JOIN)
- Derived days_of_stock using SAFE_DIVIDE(quantity, avg_daily_sales)
- Filtered to days_of_stock < 30
- Sorted by days_of_stock ascending

### Solution Code

```capybara
PIPELINE inventory_alert {
    SOURCE products: TABLE[product_id: INT?, name: STRING?, category: STRING?]
        = PARQUET(file: "input/products.parquet");
    SOURCE inventory: TABLE[product_id: INT?, quantity: INT?, avg_daily_sales: DECIMAL?]
        = PARQUET(file: "input/inventory.parquet");
    STEP joined = JOIN { TYPE INNER; ON left.product_id == right.product_id; }
    STEP with_days = DERIVE { days_of_stock = SAFE_DIVIDE(quantity, avg_daily_sales); }
    STEP urgent = FILTER { WHERE days_of_stock IS NOT NULL AND days_of_stock < 30; }
    STEP sorted = SORT { BY days_of_stock ASC; }
    SINK result = PARQUET(file: "output.parquet");
    FLOW { products -> joined.left; inventory -> joined.right; joined -> with_days -> urgent -> sorted -> result; }
}
```

